Arduino Smart Parking System

An Arduino-based Smart Parking System that uses IR sensors, a servo motor, and a 16x2 I2C LCD to automate vehicle entry/exit and display the number of available parking slots.

📌 Project Overview

The system is designed to manage a small parking area with 4 parking slots.

It uses:

Arduino UNO -- Main microcontroller

2 IR Sensors -- Detect vehicles at entry and exit

Servo Motor -- Controls the parking gate

16x2 I2C LCD -- Displays parking status

4 Parking Slots -- Initial available slot count

When a vehicle is detected at the entrance, the system checks whether a slot is available. If a slot is available, the gate opens and the available slot count decreases. When a vehicle exits, the gate opens and the available slot count increases.

