⚙️ How the System Works

Entry Process

The entry IR sensor detects a vehicle.

The Arduino checks the number of available slots.

If a slot is available, the servo opens the gate.

The available slot count decreases by 1.

The LCD displays the updated number of available slots.

The gate closes after the vehicle passes the detection sequence.

Exit Process

The exit IR sensor detects a vehicle.

The servo opens the gate.

The available slot count increases by 1.

The LCD displays the updated number of available slots.

The gate closes after the vehicle passes the detection sequence.

Parking Full

When all parking slots are occupied, the LCD displays:

SORRY :( Parking Full

The gate remains closed.

🚀 How to Run the Project

Install Arduino IDE.

Install the required libraries.

Connect the hardware according to the pin configuration.

Open system-parking-car.ino in Arduino IDE.

Select:

Tools → Board → Arduino UNO

Tools → Port → Your Arduino COM Port

Verify/compile the code.

Upload the code to the Arduino UNO.

Test the entry and exit sensors.

🔧 Important Code Note

The Arduino library headers should use the correct capitalization:

#include <Wire.h> #include <LiquidCrystal_I2C.h> #include <Servo.h>

Arduino library filenames are case-sensitive in some environments, so use the above form.

